mantle rm348
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_rowan_hazelfield
title the sparrow steps
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk sets_out_seed_on_separate_little_ledges_for_small_birds
likes hard_cheese cards tidy_house first_snow
dislikes gulls waiting
fears the_last_beak_finding_an_empty_ledge
hopes room_for_the_shyest_bird
topics animals +0.6 faith +0.5 work +0.4 food +0.2
styles comfort=make_room gossip=gentle refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# makes small seed ledges at different heights and takes particular pleasure in noticing the first timid beak at the highest one.

words
oath! = Twelve empty ledges | My scattered seeds
saying! = Feed the last beak too | A little ledge opens a wide sky
ledge = the narrow ledge | a little feeding shelf
seed = my pinch of seed | the spare grains
perch = the thin perch | a twig rest
cheese = a firm cheese heel | the yellow wedge
card = the painted card | a faded pip card
roof = a sloping cover | a small eave
cup = a grain cup | the little scoop
slot = a thumb-wide gap | the narrow opening
print = a sparrow track | a splayed print
flower = a bell of blossom | a pale flower
wax = a little warm wax | a honey-coloured curl
share = a modest heap | a small measure

any
opinion houses against 1 : A petition unanswered is bad enough. A refusal that ignores the question is a good deal harder to lay aside.
opinion church for 2 : The Bright One has room for creatures smaller than my thumb. I remember the small lives when filling a dish.
opinion dole for 2 : A generous first serving should leave a real last serving. That's what I'd ask of the dole.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : Show me the grain going into the scoop. Both of us will leave pleased with the bargain.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A shy arrival often needs an opening more than a grand welcome.
opinion road for 1 : I favour a road with a hedge broad enough for a small bird to travel alongside.

grown
line greet : Welcome. There's a free place above the bustle. | Stand in the clearer patch beside me.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A first visit deserves an easy perch. | I haven't seen you on this approach before. Welcome.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The little feet were here early. | Fresh day to you. I've just filled the first ledge.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. My eyes were on a very small arrival. | Your voice reached me through the twittering.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I'm glad to have a dear familiar face beside the ledges. | You've a standing welcome on this patch.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Hello after the little wings have folded. | The night leaves us room for a quiet greeting.
line again.open : There is still seed on the ledge from our last meeting. | You've found us receiving a second small guest.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Stand here and see who finds the upper shelf. | Come look quietly behind my shoulder.
line farewell : May your road have room for little joys. | Leave with your share of the light.
line farewell.return : A safe branch when you need one. Goodbye. | I'll leave the little place open for a return.
line react.news : I've time for the news in its own words. | My paws are free and I can attend.
line react.news.new : That hadn't reached even the edge of my hearing. | A new arrival in my thoughts altogether.
line react.news.known : I've heard that account and kept it in mind. | Yes. Same shape as the earlier news.
line react.news.doubt : I'd leave a little space open for a better account. | That seems too big a conclusion for such a little scrap.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Let me sit while you tell that. It deserves the time. | A sad empty place. I won't pretend words will fill it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : I'd put an extra pinch on the ledge for news like that. | That news will put real warmth into the prayer I say tonight.
line ask.how : Has anything small and pleasant found you today? | How are you doing for quiet company?
line answer.how : Watching a hopeful little movement over my shoulder. | Quite settled, with room for another word.
line decline : I'd leave that duty to a wolf who can give it proper attention. | I've an earlier promise to feed before I take that on.
line accept_decline : All right. An open place needn't be filled. | Then keep the bit of day you'd set aside.
line preclose : I should check which ledge is still empty. | The seed won't scatter itself evenly. I'll move along.
line accept_preclose : Of course. Go while the road looks kindly. | I'll stay and give the late arrivals a chance.
line thank : You noticed the smallest need. I appreciate it. | That was a quiet generous thing. Thank you.
line deflect_thanks : I had the seed and a ledge to put it on. | It was little effort to leave a share.
line sympathise : You can stay without saying a further word. | I've a dry place for company with a heavy heart.
line reassure : Let the smaller chance come into view first. | We've room enough to try one hopeful thing.
line ack : Yes. That little detail shows very plainly. | I follow the path of that thought.
line give.advice : Put one share away from the busiest spot. | Sit a moment after you've scattered the seed.

scene shelves
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I feed sparrows on three ledges, each a little higher. | One broad pile never fed quite as many as I thought.
b : Do they prefer the high one? | Why not spread the pile further?
a : The shyest will sometimes wait there till the bold ones are busy below. | That's exactly what the ledges do, with a clear way out behind each bird.

scene windowcrumb
when topic=animals
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Give a feeding sparrow room to leave as well as land.
b : Won't it take fright anyway? | What's behind the ledge?
a : Often enough. A clear way out lets it come back brave a second time. | Open air, if the placing is right. No kind gift ought to catch its guest in a corner.

scene hiveshift
when topic=work self.job=farmer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the grain away from the bees' busiest way to the flowers.
b : Would a sparrow bother a bee? | Do you have room for both?
a : Most won't. I prefer neither creature should have to find out when it's hungry. | A ledge at one end and a clear flight line at the other. Both get on with the day.

scene quietcheck
when topic=work self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Before lifting a hive cover I put my other work down quite out of reach.
b : Forgetting something? | Afraid the bees will object?
a : So I'll give one thing my proper attention. The seed can wait awhile. | Better for me to have steady paws and nothing loose to drop. The bees have their own duties.

scene cheesedel
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like firm cheese because one small piece sees a lengthy visit through.
b : Do the sparrows get some? | Is one piece enough dinner?
a : The little ledges get seed. I enjoy keeping the cheese myself. | With bread, yes. Especially if I have company to slow my eating down.

scene cardbird
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fancy a pack with one little bird instead of each suit mark.
b : How would you tell the high cards? | Which bird ought to win?
a : By the height of the perch. There'd be a very little picture to study on each. | I'd give the smallest one a splendid top branch. It's my pack after all.

scene firstsnow
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A fresh snow tells me instantly which ledge got its first visitor.
b : By the prints? | Wouldn't wings brush those away?
a : Two little forks of toes and a much disturbed patch beside the grain. | Sometimes. A clean shallow sweep tells nearly the same pleasant story.

scene tidyledge
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tidy the feeding shelf and leave the hedge to grow as it likes.
b : No sweeping the whole place? | Are you fond of a bit of disorder?
a : Seed hulls go. A useful tangle of twigs stays for shelter. | I like things suited to their occupants. My own room has no need of nesting twigs.

scene gullbar
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull sees a little ledge and assumes I'm preparing an enormous feast in instalments.
b : How do you persuade it otherwise? | Wouldn't it take the lot?
a : I make the perch too slight for a comfortable landing. No hard feelings required. | From a flat board, yes. That's why a twig about as thick as my claw is quite sufficient.

scene slowarrive
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I mind waiting less if I can see a tiny head coming nearer.
b : Isn't feeding all waiting? | Would you ever hurry a sparrow?
a : It's watching too. My eyes have something interesting to occupy them. | No. I save my impatience for promises made by wolves with an excellent sense of time.

scene higher_paw
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can pray with my head up while a timid bird decides whether to land.
b : What are you asking there? | Isn't that distracting?
a : Room in my own heart to be as patient with a hesitant wolf. | It helps. That little piece of life doesn't have to be taught its worth by me.

scene petition
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once sent a carefully written request a long way uphill and got a very small answer back.
b : Was the answer unfair? | Did it say what you needed?
a : It answered a different question. A refusal I could at least have understood. | No. I still have a scratch copy that makes very clear what I actually asked.

scene richscoop
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can fill a seed scoop without measuring my own supper against it. | It's easy to call a gift small when the stores behind it are ample.
b : Does that make it less worthwhile? | Do you weigh every gift?
a : No. It makes me careful about telling another wolf what ought to be affordable. | Only my own cupboard. There's enough to share without passing judgement.

scene leanweek
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When supplies shorten I give less on each ledge and keep them all in use.
b : Why not fill one properly? | Won't a small helping go quickly?
a : Because one big scuffle for a full pile does a shy hungry bird no good. | It will. I'd rather three had a taste than one got all the seed.

scene lostfacts
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I won't take an empty ledge as proof of which bird ate there.
b : Can't you recognise the marks? | Speaking about more than sparrows?
a : A print shows a visit. A strong wind can take the whole feeding away afterwards. | I am. Folk can get named as culprits on lighter evidence than a pair of bird tracks.

scene countryside
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hedge running alongside pasture can carry a whole travelling congregation of sparrows.
b : Moving through the branches? | How many would you count?
a : Yes. A little stirring follows the line of leaves and comes out singing at the end. | I don't try. I enjoy watching a hedge stir as if it had an opinion.

scene roofdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like every small feeding shelf to have a roof that doesn't shut out the sky.
b : How can a roof do both? | Planning to build them all?
a : Cover the seed by a paw's width and leave the flight path clear on two sides. | Only enough to learn which shape is actually useful. The birds usually have the last word.

scene warmwelcome
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer may like to see a place to sit before hearing all the local names.
b : You'd let introductions wait? | What if the visitor wants company?
a : Long enough to find shelter and recover a little breath. That's no disrespect. | I'd be close enough to speak with and far enough away to leave a choice.

grown

story cardshelf [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I set a bent playing card under a slightly unsteady seed dish. A gust pulled it out and carried it halfway up the hedge.
  : A sparrow settled beside it, bold as any partner I ever had.
  b : Did it play the card?
  : It played mine. I took the liberty of counting that as a win for the visiting side.

story snowfalse [topic=weather|memories]
  : One bright snow morning I found a little mark on my highest ledge like an exquisite foot. I watched a long time for its owner.
  : A drop fell from a twig end and made another foot beside it.
  b : Did you mind being deceived?
  : I minded having named the bird in my head before it was there. A patient correction did no harm.

story twoscoops [topic=food|memories]
  : I once filled my seed scoop with breakfast oats while my little breakfast bowl stood full of bird grain.
  : Noticed just as I was reaching for the cheese.
  b : Which one got the oats?
  : I did, after an exchange of vessels. The sparrows' breakfast was delayed a very reasonable minute.

rule @high
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save a pinch for the twig above the busy ledge. | Quiet. A little head at the very top.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=farmer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the bees their clear flight to the flowers. | A cover lifted gently and put back squarely.

rule @snow
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two little marks in fresh white, right by the grain. | A tiny landing spot clear of snow here.

rule @rest
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One beak more can fit on the thin perch. | A shy beak gets its own little corner.

dlg resident.hub : I've just set a pinch aside for the late birds. I'll hear you gladly.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you'd recognise that bold little shape in the hedge by now.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The small wings are quiet now. Our voices can be quiet too.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'm willing to listen if you leave the ledges and the birds alone.
dlg resident.job [self.job=farmer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I keep the way to the blossoms clear and the little ledges for birds apart.
dlg resident.job : I enjoy providing room for a small living thing to go on with its day.
dlg resident.bye : I hope some small good comes looking for you on the road.

graft resident.hub
choice Which ledge should I watch? -> shyledge
node shyledge
say The ledge beyond the busy pile. Shy birds wait there till the others are eating. Stand aside and leave the path out quite clear.
free
choice What's a good time to leave more grain? -> nextgrain
choice I'll stand back from the perch. -> hub
node nextgrain
say Once the visitors leave and I've swept the hulls clear. A heap of husks looks full to an eye in a hurry and has very little dinner in it.
choice I'll look closely at the husks. -> hub
choice I shall leave the birds in peace. -> bye
